/**
  * @description ### Precautions
  * - **Before calling this operation, ensure that you fully understand the billing methods and [pricing](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/477042.html) of Intelligent Media Management.** Each request to this operation incurs one semantic understanding fee and one query fee.
  * - Before calling this operation, ensure that you have indexed files into a dataset by binding ([CreateBinding](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/478202.html)) or active indexing ([IndexFileMeta](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/478166.html) or [BatchIndexFileMeta](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/478167.html)).
  * - The returned results are for reference only. Depending on the [workflow template configuration](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/466304.html), the categories and content of the retrieved file metadata may differ from the examples. If you have any questions, join the DingTalk group for feedback. For the DingTalk group ID, refer to [Contact us](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/84454.html).
  * ### Limits
  * - A maximum of 100 file records are returned for each query.
  * - Paged queries are not supported.
  * - Natural language understanding is not guaranteed to be completely accurate.
  * - This feature is not supported in the US (Silicon Valley) and US (Virginia) regions.
  * ### Usage
  * Use natural language keywords to search for files in a dataset. Currently, the supported key information includes labels (Labels.LabelName), time (ProduceTime), and locations (Address.AddressLine). For example, if you use `scenery in Hangzhou in 2023` as the query condition, it is intelligently split into the following three conditions to find files that meet all these conditions:
  *  - ProduceTime: From 00:00:00 on January 1, 2023 to 23:59:59 on December 31, 2023.
  * - Address.AddressLine: Contains the keyword `Hangzhou`.
  * - Labels.LabelName: Contains the `scenery` label.
  * In combination with the [workflow template configuration](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/466304.html), when the template includes the `ImageEmbeddingExtraction` operator, the search request provides content-based image search. This means the `Query` content you enter is also understood as the content contained in the image, thereby implementing intelligent image retrieval.
  * @param request  the request parameters of SemanticQuery  SemanticQueryRequest
  * @return SemanticQueryResponse
 */
async function semanticQuery(request: SemanticQueryRequest): SemanticQueryResponse {
  @handler.validateRequestModel(request);
  return @handler.do('RPC', 'SemanticQuery', 'POST', '/', 'json', false, 'json', request);
}

